 "notes": "Extracted the solid gray 'Bayesian' (conservative, full deterministic-systematics model) 95% CL joint upper limit on g_agamma from Fig. 7 (all_upper_lim.png in the e-print), the paper's final-results figure. Pixel calibration verified exactly against the CAST (6.6e-11 GeV^-1) and SN1987A (5.3e-12 GeV^-1) horizontal reference lines; extracted minimum 2.6e-13 GeV^-1 at m_a=2.9e-23 eV matches the quoted 'g<2e-13 GeV^-1 at m_a~3e-23 eV'. Mass from frequency via m_a=2*pi*hbar*nu (Eq. 5), top axis of Fig. 7. Scenario choice: the paper also shows a frequentist GLSP limit (dashed) and an 'optimistic' Bayesian limit without the deterministic-systematics fit (dotted), both cut below 2.4e-9 Hz and stronger at low mass; the conservative Bayesian solid curve is presented as the robust main result and spans the full plotted range 1e-9 to 1e-6 Hz (4.1e-24 to 4.1e-21 eV). Assumes rho_DM=0.4 GeV/cm^3 at Earth and pulsars with stochastic field amplitude effects included.",
